<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Japanese. English source quoted above each entry. Terms follow docs/i18n/ja-glossary.md.

    Android's own Japanese is used for the system features this screen talks about: サイレントモード for
    Do Not Disturb, バッテリーセーバー for Battery Saver, ワイヤレスデバッグ for Wireless debugging, and
    通知へのアクセス / 使用状況へのアクセス for the two special accesses, so that the wording matches the
    Settings screens these buttons open.

    The adb command lines themselves are constants in code and appear untranslated between these
    captions, which is why the ADB card's prose refers to "1 行目" rather than quoting the command.
-->
